            <ArticleTitle>Continuous vancomycin in a pediatric cystic fibrosis patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E4-E5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ppul.23844</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Continuous vancomycin has been previously reported to maximize antimicrobial activity while avoiding toxicities associated with dose escalation, but the efficacy of this dosing strategy has not been reported. This case report describes the successful use of continuous vancomycin, including improvement in lung function and avoidance of nephrotoxicity, demonstrated in a pediatric cystic fibrosis (CF) patient with MRSA.</AbstractText>
